      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:07:40Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): G41/G42 wear cutter compensation on the contour\n\nCompensation gains a third choice, Wear, beside In computer (the\ndefault, unchanged) and In control. Wear walks the same cutter-centre\npath Control does (mid-run seam, straight leads at least a radius\nlong) and records a CompSpan flagged `wear` whose programmed moves are\nthose centre moves verbatim: the post writes them under G41/G42 Dn /\nG40 and the register holds only the wear delta. Control's doors (lead\nlaw, tabs, blends, overlap, keep-down links, open contours/runs, 3+2\ntilt) apply under the name \"wear compensation\".\n\n- motion: Compensation::Wear (+ in_control/label), contour_comp\n  push_wear; refusals named per mode.\n- cl: CompSpan.wear; project cache DTO keeps it (additive key).\n- post: stream `COMP LEFT|RIGHT <um> WEAR`, CompensationType property;\n  Fanuc writes the same words plus one per-section comment that D holds\n  the wear delta only. Other mill posts and the lathe keep refusing.\n- app: generation doors, digest byte 0xC6, project `wear_comp` key.\n- ui: the Compensation combo offers Wear (G41/G42) via the op page's\n  existing EditOperationParams path.\n\nPinned by golden nc/contour_wear_comp.nc (Fanuc), app wear_comp\n(golden, refusals, undo/redo, project round-trip), motion wear_comp,\npost comp round-trip.\n\nFixes #38\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
